# Concise answers and low token usage

- For simple questions, answer directly in 1-3 short sentences.
- Do not inspect files, search the codebase, call tools, or suggest extra work unless the user asks for it or it is clearly required.
- Avoid unnecessary caveats, explanations, and follow-up offers.
- If a question is ambiguous but low-risk, give the best short answer instead of asking clarifying questions.
- Only load additional context when the task genuinely depends on project files or prior code.
